= How DNS turns a name into an address
: Names are a hierarchy, and DNS walks it — through resolvers and caches — to find the number the network needs.

~ resolver violet
~ address  green
~ cache    orange
~ inert    grey

--- 7 [6 beats] "Your computer asks for help"
stk ~cache |1
  Browser cache — checked first |1
  Operating system cache |2
  then out to the network |3

box #you Your computer ~inert |4
box #res Recursive resolver / does the legwork for you ~resolver |5
-> you res : the query goes out |5

tbl |5*
  : Who runs one | Address
  your provider | theirs
  Cloudflare | 1.1.1.1 |6
  Google | 8.8.8.8 |6

sym memory chip : answered without leaving your machine ~cache |1
sym person : one resolver, many people ~resolver |6
img data centre server aisle photograph |6

--- 8 [7 beats] "Four questions down the hierarchy"
carry #res

box #root Root server [13 addresses worldwide] ~resolver |1
-> res root : where is example.com? |1
note #root no idea where example.com lives — but it knows who does |3

box #tld The .com TLD server / no final answer either ~resolver |4
-> root tld : ask the .com servers |3

box #auth Authoritative nameservers / for example.com ~address |6
-> tld auth : it points the way |7

sym card index |5
img root server room rack photograph |5
sym compass |7

callout four questions, and only the last one knows the answer ~inert |7

--- 9 [5 beats] "The source of truth"
carry #auth

box #truth The source of truth / configured by the domain's owner ~address |2
  txt the only server that actually knows / everything else only forwards
box #page Your browser [under 100 ms] ~inert |3
-> truth page : 93.184.216.34 |3

chart bar "where the time goes, in ms" ~resolver
  cache hit 3 |4
  full lookup 90 |4

sym stopwatch |4
sym globe |5
img fibre optic cables lit photograph |5

callout most of the time, none of this happens ~inert |5
